From: illumos-drm <illumos-drm@code.aopc.cloud>
Subject: [PATCH 12] i915: mode setting through misc/drm_kms

On illumos the DRM core (misc/drm_core) owns the ioctl entry, files and
events, and forwards the mode-setting ioctls of a Linux-KMS device to
Linux's KMS code, which misc/drm_kms carries (facade 2.0, drm_lkms.h).
The display build of i915n (compiled with -DI915N_DISPLAY: build.sh's
I915_DISPLAY=1, the default) points the driver table's illumos_lkms at
i915n's copy of misc/drm_kms' hook table (drm_kms_illumos_funcs, with
lastclose also restoring the illumos console). The core
uses it only if the device still has DRIVER_MODESET when the LinuxKPI
layer's drm_dev_register() starts mode setting: a platform without
display (patch 0011) has cleared it by then and stays headless. The
headless build (I915_DISPLAY=0, no I915N_DISPLAY) leaves the hook out
and does not link against misc/drm_kms.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/i915_driver.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/i915_driver.c
@@ -1888,11 +1888,23 @@
 #define DRIVER_MAJOR		1
 #define DRIVER_MINOR		6
 #define DRIVER_PATCHLEVEL	0
+
+#if defined(__illumos__) && defined(I915N_DISPLAY)
+/*
+ * misc/drm_kms: Linux's KMS code behind the DRM core (facade 2.0); i915n's
+ * copy of its hook table also restores the illumos console at lastclose
+ * (illumos/i915_illumos_con_kms.c).
+ */
+extern struct drm_illumos_lkms_funcs i915n_lkms_funcs;
+#endif
 
 static const struct drm_driver i915_drm_driver = {
 #ifdef __illumos__
 	DRM_FACADE_DRIVER_VERSION,
 #endif
+#if defined(__illumos__) && defined(I915N_DISPLAY)
+	.illumos_lkms = &i915n_lkms_funcs,
+#endif
 	.driver_features =
 	    DRIVER_GEM |
 	    DRIVER_RENDER | DRIVER_MODESET | DRIVER_ATOMIC | DRIVER_SYNCOBJ |
